  "pr": {
    "description": "This PR adds generic support for defining or referencing secure values withiin any resource.  It adds a top level \\"secure\\" section that lives next to \\"spec\\". (alternativly we could consider making it a property on spec, but that may lead to weird behaviors depending on how spec is defined)\\r\\n\\r\\nConsider a resource like:\\r\\n\`\`\`\\r\\napiVersion: testdata.datasource.grafana.app/v0alpha1\\r\\nkind: DataSource\\r\\nmetadata:\\r\\n  name: sample-testdata\\r\\nspec:\\r\\n  title: Sample datasource\\r\\n  url: http://...\\r\\nsecure:\\r\\n  sampleA:\\r\\n    create: secret value here # replaced with a name on write\\r\\n  sampleB:\\r\\n    name: XYZ # reference to a existing secret\\r\\n\`\`\`\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen writing to unistore, this will automatically process the secure section so any raw values are replaced with a reference:\\r\\n\\r\\n\`\`\`mermaid\\r\\nsequenceDiagram\\r\\n    autonumber\\r\\n    actor User\\r\\n    participant apistore\\r\\n    participant secrets\\r\\n    participant unistore\\r\\n\\r\\n    User->>apistore: Update resource<br>with secrets\\r\\n    apistore->>secrets: CreateInline A\\r\\n    apistore->>secrets: CreateInline B\\r\\n    apistore->>unistore: Create/Update/Delete\\r\\n    unistore->>secrets: CanReference\\r\\n    apistore->>secrets: DeleteInline C<br>(if required from changes)\\r\\n    apistore->>User: success\\r\\n\`\`\`\\r\\n\\r\\nThe apistore is responsible for managing the inline secrets explicitly -- eventually we will likely have a garbage collector for secrets, but that should only be required when create succeeds, but the following Write requests to unistore fail",
    "number": 107803,
